WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.571
Watch the supplied fox run, using its existing animation.

00:00:03.711 --> 00:00:07.679
Four synchronized views reveal different aspects of the same moving pose.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.592
Mint tracks the front foot; apricot tracks the tail in profile.

00:00:11.732 --> 00:00:14.143
Each trail shows where that bone was a moment ago.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.291
Slow the run and watch how the two paths curve.

00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:20.991
Match those lines to the legs and tail in each view.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.227
Freeze here and look at the shape of each path.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.204
Then watch the run start again as both trails move on.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.827
The fox runs in place, so these lines do not show real travel.

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:38.463
They track bones, not footprints or ground forces.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.912
Use the trail to find a moment, then inspect that pose in each view.

00:00:44.052 --> 00:00:45.588
One clue can guide the next check.
